{"action_id":null,"arguments":[],"assumptions":[{"assumption_id":"node.b66b3e831bb98a12db59dffa.a0","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The assessment concerns one identified material post-authorisation investment change to an SFC-authorised fund within the circular’s UCITS definition.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.b66b3e831bb98a12db59dffa.a1","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"All product features involved in the identified change are assessed; the source supplies no rule for severing a bundled change.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.b66b3e831bb98a12db59dffa.a2","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"28 November 2025 governs commencement of the removal measure.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.b66b3e831bb98a12db59dffa.a3","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The transition preserves the process for an existing application; it does not expressly make application history an additional substantive exception to the removal measure.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.b66b3e831bb98a12db59dffa.a4","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Substantive qualification for removal does not establish permission to bypass a preserved application process or establish overall legal compliance.","status":"PROVISIONAL"}],"bundle_hash":"87a2b103adc1f70a21ebe4a5f2caf045f9de460ade098c4cf6e809b56b2cf6e9","candidate_id":"candidate.2ef3ba2cf8cc4a909781bc04fa95fad0","controlled_language":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] Within scope, true means the identified change satisfies the substantive home-requirements and exception tests in item (ii); false means at least one of those tests fails. The result answers only that substantive question. It does not answer whether a pending application can leave the existing process or whether prior approval is legally required in the particular procedural circumstances. Outside scope no conclusion is supplied. Unknown facts remain unknown. This proposal confers no legal approval.","disposition_reason":"Unreviewed interpretation proposal","family_ids":["dependencies"],"generation_phase":"BLIND_INITIAL","issue_ids":["issue.68376e39217f49c4be6b4ab42222a92c","issue.0074fdb7d4324fefa2b1cf8f77d2685c","issue.c7508f9de0b04ac0a85fb1037326c797","issue.15be0aa3a05f4fc98bdf697b59498ab2","issue.79552d8d99f146e69be2408a24719903"],"parent_id":null,"probability_of_legal_correctness":null,"revision_reason":"Both prior models turn existence of a pending pre-effective application into a change-level removal veto. This rival distinguishes the substantive conditions attached to a change from the process attached to an application. A substantively qualifying change can coexist with an application that must follow the existing process. The prior models already identify the main actors and feature quantifiers; the consequential issue is the relation between application history and the legal effect being computed, including later application decisions.","run_id":"run.57127ace1fc14bbe97f783a02f719446","scheduling_priority":0,"schema_version":"interpretation.v1","score_purpose":"INVESTIGATION_PRIORITY_ONLY","source_packet_hash":"6c557525c251e4c0794c0061ba5b7f7fec9be45d9495dd1ca07063f018b43c06","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u10.1809","d97b56331f41a.u17.2556","d97b56331f41a.u3.575","d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"],"status":"ACTIVE","subject_unit":"Substantive removal conditions distinguished from preservation of an application’s existing process"}